  "elevationPhilosophy": "The system deliberately avoids shadow. Layer separation comes from three tools only: (1) the Fog Gray #f9f9f9 card surface one step above the white canvas, (2) pastel color washes that re-zone sections, and (3) 1px Ash Border hairlines. There is no box-shadow token, no hover lift, no glow — depth is communicated through color temperature and surface tint shifts, not elevation. This keeps the interface feeling flat, friendly, and editorial rather than skeuomorphic.",
  "imagery": "Lifestyle photography dominates: candid shots of real dogs and their owners in natural-light, high-key environments (a woman kneeling with a doodle on a pink seamless, a small dog with a toothbrush mid-chew). No staged studio backdrops, no product-only hero shots — the dog or owner is always part of the composition. Product photography appears on flat color backdrops that match the SKU flavor (yellow, teal, lavender) rather than the brand palette, letting the product feel like a distinct object. Icons are minimal and mono — only the green checkmark bullet appears repeatedly. No illustrations, no 3D renders, no abstract graphics. Imagery fills roughly 50% of the page on the hero and shrinks to 30% in product sections. Images are cropped tight and often bleed edge-to-edge in their containers.",
  "layout": "Max-width 1280px centered container with generous side padding. The hero is a full-bleed Blush Petal band with a 50/50 split: left column holds the 64–96px headline and two pill CTAs stacked above a feature bullet; right column is a full-bleed lifestyle image. Sections alternate full-width pastel bands (blush → white → sky-blue → white → midnight-navy) with 80px vertical gaps between bands. Content within sections is 2-column (text+image) or 3-column (product card grid), never masonry. Navigation is a thin top bar (60–70px) centered on a 3-zone layout: left cluster (Shop + Take Quiz links), centered wordmark logo, right cluster (account + cart icons). Sticky on scroll. The dark endorsement section breaks the pattern with inverted contrast but keeps the same 2-column rhythm. Density is comfortable — sections breathe, never crammed, and whitespace does most of the layout work.",
